{
  "_comment": [
    "CodeArena sandbox seccomp profile.",
    "",
    "This REPLACES Docker's default profile rather than extending it -- the runtime has no",
    "notion of layering -- so it is an allowlist: anything not named below returns EPERM.",
    "That posture is deliberate. A denylist would let a syscall added by a future kernel",
    "through by default, which is the failure mode that matters for a sandbox.",
    "",
    "HOW THIS LIST WAS BUILT",
    "  From observed requirements, not from guesswork about what looks dangerous. The",
    "  allowlist was validated by actually compiling and running C++, Java and Python",
    "  programs under it; SandboxSeccompIT keeps doing so, so a name removed by accident",
    "  fails the build rather than a submission.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS DENIED, AND WHY IT MATTERS",
    "  ptrace, process_vm_readv/writev, kcmp   - inspecting or altering another process",
    "  mount, umount2, pivot_root, chroot,     - rearranging the filesystem view, the",
    "  move_mount, fsopen, fsconfig, fsmount,    classic route out of a container",
    "  fspick, open_tree, mount_setattr",
    "  name_to_handle_at, open_by_handle_at    - opening a file by inode, which escapes a",
    "                                            chroot/mount-namespace confinement",
    "  unshare, setns                          - entering or creating namespaces",
    "  bpf, perf_event_open, userfaultfd       - kernel-facing attack surface with a long",
    "                                            history of privilege-escalation bugs",
    "  init_module, finit_module,              - loading kernel code",
    "  delete_module, create_module,",
    "  query_module, get_kernel_syms",
    "  kexec_load, kexec_file_load, reboot     - taking the machine down",
    "  add_key, request_key, keyctl            - the kernel keyring",
    "  io_uring_setup/enter/register           - a large, young, and repeatedly exploited",
    "                                            asynchronous-IO interface this needs none of",
    "  capset                                  - acquiring capabilities (capget is allowed:",
    "                                            reading them is harmless)",
    "  pidfd_getfd                             - stealing a file descriptor from another",
    "                                            process",
    "  swapon, swapoff, quotactl, acct,        - system administration",
    "  syslog, settimeofday, clock_settime,",
    "  clock_adjtime, adjtimex, nfsservctl,",
    "  ioperm, iopl, modify_ldt, uselib,",
    "  ustat, sysfs, _sysctl, lookup_dcookie,",
    "  vm86, vm86old",
    "",
    "WHAT IS NOT DONE HERE",
    "  Networking syscalls (socket, connect, sendto, ...) are ALLOWED. Network isolation is",
    "  enforced by --network none, which gives the container no interface to use, and that",
    "  is a stronger and much less brittle control than filtering syscalls: the JVM and",
    "  CPython both create sockets during normal startup, and denying socket() breaks them",
    "  for no gain. A connect() in this sandbox fails because there is nowhere to connect",
    "  to, and SandboxIsolationIT proves that by running a program that tries.",
    "",
    "  Nothing here substitutes for the capability drop, the read-only filesystem, the",
    "  cgroup limits or the network namespace. It is one layer among several."
  ],
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
  "archMap": [
    {
